WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:06.239
Your team is spread around the world. Do you know what it's like where they are,

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:06.996
right now?

00:00:07.743 --> 00:00:12.604
A list of names and time zones tells you almost nothing. Is it morning there? Is it

00:00:12.604 --> 00:00:14.368
raining? Are they asleep?

00:00:15.486 --> 00:00:20.056
Meet Mondino. Your team, around the world, right now, on one little globe.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:27.953
Start a team in a minute: a team name, your name, a work email, a country and a

00:00:27.953 --> 00:00:28.971
postal code.

00:00:29.316 --> 00:00:32.970
Then Mondino hands you an invite link, to bring everyone in.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:39.984
A teammate opens the link, and sees the team already on the globe.

00:00:40.329 --> 00:00:44.960
They type a postal code. Mondino finds the city and the weather there, and the

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:46.923
button says: Join Northwind.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.848
Only the city is ever shown. The postal code stays private, and nobody sees an

00:00:53.848 --> 00:00:54.641
address.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:01:01.594
Coming back on another device? There is no password. Mondino emails a link that

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:04.514
signs you in, once, within fifteen minutes.

00:01:07.104 --> 00:01:12.053
Then, the globe. Lit and shaded in three dimensions, with the night side in dusk.

00:01:12.398 --> 00:01:15.778
It turns slowly on its own, and you can drag it to spin.

00:01:17.428 --> 00:01:21.842
Every pin is a person, their clock and their sky: initials in their own colour,

00:01:21.842 --> 00:01:24.154
local time, weather and temperature.

00:01:24.499 --> 00:01:27.374
Teammates who are close together share one group pin.

00:01:30.332 --> 00:01:33.308
Select a pin, and the globe turns to that teammate.

00:01:33.653 --> 00:01:38.313
You see their city, their local time, how far ahead or behind they are, their status

00:01:38.313 --> 00:01:39.611
and their weather.

00:01:39.957 --> 00:01:42.715
And the working hours you share, on your own clock.

00:01:45.818 --> 00:01:51.148
Status comes from the local hour: early morning, working hours, evening, or probably

00:01:51.148 --> 00:01:53.732
asleep. No tracking. Just the clock.

00:01:56.141 --> 00:02:00.988
With no pin selected, the panel counts teammates and time zones, and lists who is in

00:02:00.988 --> 00:02:02.673
working hours right now.

00:02:06.465 --> 00:02:10.702
The Team page shows where everyone is in their day. A day ribbon places each

00:02:10.702 --> 00:02:13.510
teammate at the hour they are living through.

00:02:13.855 --> 00:02:18.442
Below it, everyone from west to east, filtered by working now, or asleep.

00:02:21.951 --> 00:02:27.288
It scales, too. A team of five hundred is drawn as group pins, each with a count.

00:02:32.274 --> 00:02:37.821
Invite teammate opens the team's invite link, with one button to copy it. No admins,

00:02:37.821 --> 00:02:38.979
and no roles.

00:02:42.598 --> 00:02:47.456
And it fits every screen: a phone, a tablet, a desktop, in light and in dark.

00:02:52.922 --> 00:02:58.062
Coming next: Moments, for holidays, races and local events where teammates live; and

00:02:58.062 --> 00:03:00.749
Profile and Settings, for your own pin.

00:03:03.245 --> 00:03:06.275
Mondino. Your team, around the world, right now.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:10.305
Mondino is where a team spread around the world sees each other.

00:03:10.650 --> 00:03:16.310
A teammate joins with a postal code and appears as a pin on an interactive 3D globe.

00:03:16.655 --> 00:03:21.498
Each pin shows that teammate's local time, temperature and weather, and a playful

00:03:21.498 --> 00:03:26.461
highlight when something is happening where they live: a local holiday, a Formula 1

00:03:26.461 --> 00:03:27.778
race, a festival.
